    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0510" n="1244" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1244"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 512.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to your No. 409, of April 4,
                    regarding an apprehended massacre of Christians in Turkey, and the proposed
                    visit of the <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> to Smyrna, Alexandretta,
                    and Beirut, I have to inform you that for the last three weeks tranquility seems
                    to exist in the provinces, and I see no cause to fear present danger. The
                    pledges given me for energetic official action, I feel sure, have been complied
                    with.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
